    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d233">

                <pb facs="0412" n="372" sameAs="frus:frus1865p1/pg372"/>

                <head>Mr. Hunter to Mr. Adams</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1418.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-05-22"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >May</hi> 22, 1865</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> There are no events of sufficient
                    importance to mention since the last weekly summary, that are not clearly stated
                    in the official bulletin of the War Department published in the Chronicle
                    newspaper, the files of which are now regularly forwarded to all of our
                    legations. The Stonewall at last advices was at Havana, and energetic measures
                    have been adopted with a view to her capture or destruction.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. HUNTER, <hi rendition="#italic">Acting
                    Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                    <p>[Same, <hi rendition="#italic">mutatis mutandis,</hi> to all our principal
                        ministers in Europe.]</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
